  "ref": "DEU.10.10",
  "review_notes": [
    "*as at the first time* gives *as at* to kĕ as one compound rendering (rule 30); the competing reading marks *at* added, which would leave a word the ASV wrote answering to no morpheme in a phrase where the preposition is present.",
    "In *that time also* the ASV drops the preposition's relation entirely, so bĕ and its assimilated article are unrepresented while the demonstrative takes the written determiner."
  ]
